{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_38","type":"agent_message","text":"The mitigation is submitted and was accepted at the mitigation stage.\n\n**Root cause:** The `recommendation` Service had `internalTrafficPolicy: Local`. Its only pod runs on `kind-worker`, so requests from pods on other nodes timed out. That caused frontend-proxy `/api/recommendations` calls to return 504s.\n\n**Fix:** I patched the Service to `internalTrafficPolicy: Cluster`, the default that the other services use. Cross-node connections to `recommendation:8080` now succeed, and a test request through frontend-proxy returned 200 in under a second.\n\nI left `otel-collector` on `Local` because that is intentional for the per-node agent DaemonSet. I also left the `nodeSelector` pinning `recommendation` to `kind-worker` in place. It is not what caused the outage, but it could reintroduce single-node scheduling risk if that node fails."}}
